1780272000,22.89],[1782864000,23.7],[1785542400,13.9]]}]}],"qna":[{"question":"What is the significance of the Two Wheeler Sales data?","answer":"Sales data for two wheelers in India is a vital indicator for understanding broader economic conditions within the services sector activities, both in urban and rural areas, particularly in the context of middle-class and rural populations, where these vehicles play a crucial role in personal mobility and delivery services.^The data offers insights into consumer preferences, transportation needs, and job stability especially in urban areas and disposable income of rural populations."},{"question":"How to interpret the Two Wheeler Sales data?","answer":"A rise in Two Wheeler sales may indicate increased demand for personal transportation, and vice versa.^The auto and automotive industry is cyclical, with sales often influenced by factors such as festive seasons, end-of-year discounts, and new model launches. Thus, analysing the monthly cumulative sales data on a year-on-year basis (total data from the beginning of the fiscal year) is advisable to overcome any seasonal fluctuations.^Trends in two wheeler sales can be correlated with other economic indicators, such as fuel prices, interest rates on vehicle loans, and overall economic growth, providing a comprehensive view of the economy."},{"question":"What does the Two Wheeler Sales data represent?","answer":"This data represents the sale of key modes of transport, such as two-wheelers (motorcycles, scooters, mopeds), within India encompassing different brands, engine capacities, electric and conventional fuel types.^The data helps in understanding the dynamics of the auto and automotive market in India, particularly in the context of urban and rural transportation."}],"related":[{"slug":"average-daily-electronic-toll-collection","title":"E-Toll Collections (Daily Avg)"},{"slug":"bank-credit-growth","title":"Bank Credit Growth"},{"slug":"capacity-utilisation","title":"Capacity Utilisation"},{"slug":"cement-production","title":"Cement Production"},{"slug":"crude-oil-price-indian-basket","title":"Crude Oil Price (Indian Basket)"},{"slug":"domestic-passenger-car-sales","title":"Domestic Passenger Car Sales"},{"slug":"domestic-tractor-sales","title":"Domestic Tractor Sales"},{"slug":"energy-requirements","title":"Energy Requirements"},{"slug":"essential-commodity-prices","title":"Essential Commodity Prices"},{"slug":"goods-and-services-tax-gst-collections","title":"GST Collections"},{"slug":"money-supply-m3","title":"Money Supply (M3)"},{"slug":"natural-gas-production","title":"Natural Gas Production"},{"slug":"non-oil-exports","title":"Non-Oil Exports"},{"slug":"petroleum-consumption","title":"Petroleum Consumption"},{"slug":"private-consumption-pfce","title":"Private Consumption (PFCE)"},{"slug":"revenue-earnings-railway-freight-traffic-major-commodities","title":"Railway Freight Traffic- Revenue"},{"slug":"steel-consumption","title":"Steel Consumption"},{"slug":"steel-production","title":"Steel Production"}],"title":"Domestic Two-Wheeler Sales","description":"India's domestic two-wheeler sales stand at 2,590 Thousand for Aug 2026. Two-wheelers are more exposed to rural income trends than cars.","headline":{"Absolute":"India's domestic two-wheeler sales stand at 2,590 Thousand for Aug 2026. Two-wheelers are more exposed to rural income trends than cars.","Y-o-Y":"India's domestic two-wheeler sales stand at 13.90% for Aug 2026. Two-wheelers are more exposed to rural income trends than cars."},"source":"CMIE Economic Outlook, 1 Finance Research","source_url":"https://economicoutlook.cmie.com/","date_modified":"2026-08-01","scraped_at":"2026-10-13T15:27:40+00:00"}